.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-COMMAND-CENTER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-command-center
.Nd four Grafana dashboards on four desktop workspaces, from one key
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm urls | stop | status
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Ctrl+Delete, bound by kldload's GNOME workspace-keys extension, asks
.Nm
for four dashboard addresses and opens one window on each workspace:
the network, ZFS pool health, the Kubernetes lifecycle, and the host.
A dashboard that cannot be found falls back to Grafana's list of
dashboards, so there are always four.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm urls
The four addresses, in workspace order, one a line.
.It Cm stop
Close every command-center window.
.It Cm status
.Ql running
or
.Ql stopped .
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_CC_GRAFANA
Grafana's address; default
.Ql http://localhost:3000 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 when a step failed; 2 on a usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ kldload-command-center urls
http://localhost:3000/grafana/d/kldload-network-live/4188070?kiosk&refresh=30s
http://localhost:3000/grafana/d/zfs-pool-health/storage-e28094-zfs-pool-health?kiosk&refresh=30s
http://localhost:3000/grafana/d/kldload-k8s-lifecycle/6dea608?kiosk&refresh=30s
http://localhost:3000/grafana/d/rYdddlPWk/host-full-e28094-every-system-metric?kiosk&refresh=30s
# (exited 0)
$ kldload-command-center status
stopped
# (exited 0)
.Ed
